WHAT THIS FILE IS

  This file lists third-party material that LMDS derives from, or may include.
  It exists so that attribution and license text are in place *before* any such
  material is incorporated, not scrambled together afterwards.

  Each entry records the project name, its URL, its license type, and the exact
  copyright line that must travel with its code.

  This file covers third-party *software* only. It does NOT cover:

    - model weights, container images and runtimes that LMDS merely downloads
      or launches at deploy time (vLLM, llama.cpp, Hugging Face repositories,
      NGC images). Those are covered by their own licenses and are neither
      included in nor distributed with LMDS. See LICENSE / NOTICE.
    - LMDS's own code, which is proprietary. See LICENSE.

CURRENT STATUS — READ THIS

  As of the "Last reviewed" date above, **no code has been copied into LMDS
  from any project listed below.** Every entry is currently marked either
  "no code incorporated" or "reference only".

  The list is published anyway, deliberately: the moment a line of code from
  one of these projects lands in this repository, the attribution is already
  here and correct, and only the status line has to change.

"REFERENCE ONLY" MEANS FACTS, NOT CODE

  Some entries are marked "reference only". Those projects contributed
  *facts* to LMDS's recipe catalog — flag names, image tags, measured
  throughput, context limits, parser names, known-bad settings. Facts are not
  copyrightable subject matter, so no license obligation attaches to them and
  no MIT notice is required for a fact.

  What IS copyrightable in those repositories is their prose: README text,
  code comments, explanations, and the expression of their scripts. None of
  that has been copied, and none of it may be pasted into catalog `notes:`
  fields or documentation.

  Where LMDS uses a fact from one of these projects, the recipe entry carries
  `source:` and `validated_on:` pointing at the origin. That is provenance
  and honesty, not a license obligation.

MAINTENANCE RULE

  When code from a listed project is actually incorporated:

    1. change that entry's Status line to "INCORPORATED", naming the specific
       LMDS files involved and what was taken;
    2. add a provenance header to each derived file — upstream URL, upstream
       license, upstream copyright line, and what was changed;
    3. keep the copyright line below byte-for-byte identical to the upstream
       original.

  When a project is added, add it here in the same shape before merging.

